MIGraphX (pinned tag rocm-7.14): declare/define gfx_default_rocblas()
unconditionally, instead of only under `#if MIGRAPHX_USE_HIPBLASLT`, so
the build compiles with hipBLASLt disabled -- the only configuration any
non-gfx90a/gfx94x/gfx95x/gfx110x/gfx120x target (gfx803 included) can
build in, since hipBLASLt has no kernels for anything else.

WHY
---
src/targets/gpu/lowering.cpp calls `gpu::gfx_default_rocblas()`
unconditionally (no `#if MIGRAPHX_USE_HIPBLASLT` around the call site
itself):

    not hipblaslt_supported() or gpu::gfx_default_rocblas())

But `gfx_default_rocblas()`'s only declaration (device_name.hpp) and
definition (device_name.cpp) are both wrapped in
`#if MIGRAPHX_USE_HIPBLASLT`. With hipBLASLt off (`-DMIGRAPHX_USE_HIPBLASLT
=Off`, required on gfx803 -- hipBLASLt has never had gfx8 kernels, see
gfx803/EVALUATION_ROCM_7.md's hipBLASLt section), the symbol simply
doesn't exist and lowering.cpp fails to compile: "no member named
'gfx_default_rocblas' in namespace 'migraphx::gpu'". This is a real
upstream gap in the rocm-7.14 source, not a gfx803-specific issue -- it
would reproduce for any target built with hipBLASLt disabled. Confirmed
directly against the pinned tag's source, not assumed.

The call is dead code once hipBLASLt is compiled out, not just at
runtime on this hardware: `hipblaslt_supported()` itself is `#if
!MIGRAPHX_USE_HIPBLASLT return false; #else ...`, so with HIPBLASLT off
it always returns false, and `not hipblaslt_supported()` is always true
-- the `or gpu::gfx_default_rocblas()` after it never actually
evaluates due to short-circuit `or`. The symbol only needs to exist for
the translation unit to compile; its return value is unreachable in
this build configuration.

WHAT
----
Move the two `gfx_default_rocblas()` declarations in device_name.hpp
outside the `#if MIGRAPHX_USE_HIPBLASLT` guard so they're always
visible. In device_name.cpp, keep the real HIPBLASLT-on implementation
as-is and add an `#else` branch defining both overloads to return
`true` -- matching the function's ordinary "prefer rocblas over
hipblaslt" meaning (there being no hipblaslt at all is the strongest
case for preferring rocblas), even though this branch is unreachable
given hipblaslt_supported()'s own false-when-disabled behavior.

Applies to: MIGraphX @ rocm-7.14 tag, any GPU_TARGETS built with
MIGRAPHX_USE_HIPBLASLT=Off -- not gfx803-specific in what it touches,
gfx803 is simply the target that surfaced it here. See
gfx-default-rocblas-hipblaslt-off-build-failure.sh for how this patch
is applied and verified at build time.

diff --git a/src/targets/gpu/device_name.cpp b/src/targets/gpu/device_name.cpp
index 2b825ea..5c162af 100644
--- a/src/targets/gpu/device_name.cpp
+++ b/src/targets/gpu/device_name.cpp
@@ -143,6 +143,22 @@ static bool hipblaslt_supported_impl(const std::string& gfx_name)
             (starts_with(gfx_name, "gfx95") and gfx_name >= "gfx950") or
             starts_with(gfx_name, "gfx110") or starts_with(gfx_name, "gfx120"));
 }
+
+#else
+
+// GFX_DEFAULT_ROCBLAS_HIPBLASLT_OFF_PATCH: with hipBLASLt compiled out
+// entirely, rocblas is the only GEMM provider there is -- these two
+// overloads are unreachable in practice (hipblaslt_supported() below
+// always returns false in this build, so lowering.cpp's short-circuit
+// `not hipblaslt_supported() or gfx_default_rocblas()` never evaluates
+// them) but must still exist for the translation unit to link.
+bool gfx_default_rocblas() { return true; }
+bool gfx_default_rocblas(const context& ctx)
+{
+    (void)ctx;
+    return true;
+}
+
 #endif
 
 bool hipblaslt_supported()
diff --git a/src/targets/gpu/include/migraphx/gpu/device_name.hpp b/src/targets/gpu/include/migraphx/gpu/device_name.hpp
index 7d8f965..a51f771 100644
--- a/src/targets/gpu/include/migraphx/gpu/device_name.hpp
+++ b/src/targets/gpu/include/migraphx/gpu/device_name.hpp
@@ -55,10 +55,8 @@ MIGRAPHX_GPU_EXPORT bool gfx_has_mx_intrinsics(const context& ctx);
 
 MIGRAPHX_GPU_EXPORT bool gfx_has_fp8fnuz_support();
 
-#if MIGRAPHX_USE_HIPBLASLT
 MIGRAPHX_GPU_EXPORT bool gfx_default_rocblas();
 MIGRAPHX_GPU_EXPORT bool gfx_default_rocblas(const context& ctx);
-#endif
 
 MIGRAPHX_GPU_EXPORT bool hipblaslt_supported();
 MIGRAPHX_GPU_EXPORT bool hipblaslt_supported(const context& ctx);
